  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f,g$ be continuous functions from $[0,\\infty)$ to itself, $h(x)=\\int_{2x}^{3x}f(t)\\,dt$, and $F(x)=\\int_0^{h(x)}g(t)\\,dt$. If $F^\\prime$ is the derivative of $F$, then for $x>0$",
  "options": {
    "A": "$F^\\prime(x)=g(h(x))$",
    "B": "$F^\\prime(x)=g(h(x))[f(3x)-f(2x)]$",
    "C": "$F^\\prime(x)=g(h(x))[3xf(3x)-2xf(2x)]$",
    "D": "$F^\\prime(x)=g(h(x))[3xf(3x)\\ln3-2xf(2x)\\ln2]$"
  },
